{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויעזקהו.</b> Some say it is from the Aramaic translation of טבעת (Isaiah 3:21) — עזקתא, but this has no basis. The correct view is that this word has no cognate [in Hebrew]; it is found only in the language of Kedar, and its meaning is like a fence and a hedge." "<b>ויסקלהו.</b> From the heavy [binyan] stem, and its meaning is to remove the stones. If it were from the light [binyan] stem, then it would mean to gather the stones, and likewise ושרשך מארץ חיים (Psalms 52:7)." "<b>ויטעהו שורק.</b> From [the root of] שורק, for the verbal noun has the force of every verb, past or future." "<b>ויבן מגדל בתוכו.</b> A place for the watchman to sit." "<b>וגם יקב חצב בו.</b> To draw out the must from the vineyard." "<b>באושים.</b> Like thorns, like ותחת שעורה באשה (Job 31:40)." "And the meaning of <b>ויעזקהו</b> is that the land of Israel was built with fine houses and walls, and ויסקלהו, that he drove out the Canaanites, and the tower is the House of HaShem that was on Mount Moriah, and the winepress is a parable for the altar of burnt offering; grapes are like the righteous."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:12.025166487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}